# Patterns here are matched against paths relative to the build context
# (`apps/api`), and a pattern without `**/` matches ONLY at the top level.
# `__pycache__/` alone therefore let `migrations/__pycache__` into the migrate
# image — the root .dockerignore carries both forms for exactly this reason.
.venv/
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
**/*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
tests/
*.md
